INSERT INTO "public"."articles" ("id", "title", "slug", "content", "excerpt", "author_id", "category_id", "cover_image", "status", "published_at", "created_at", "updated_at", "article_type", "featured", "submitted_for_review_at", "reviewed_by", "review_notes") VALUES
	('b7c77d43-7934-42f5-939c-b40bcd450445', 'Featured Article: Title Goes Here (Sample Item)', 'featured-article-title-goes-here-sample-item-92241092-inu03', '<h1>You Can Help Save the Planet! 🌍</h1><p><em>How Kids Can Make a Big Difference in the Fight Against Climate Change</em></p><p>Did you know that kids all around the world are helping to protect our planet? Even small actions can make a big difference when it comes to climate change!</p><h2>🌱 What is Climate Change?</h2><p>Climate change means the Earth is getting warmer because of pollution and too much carbon dioxide (CO2) in the air. This causes problems like hotter days, stronger storms, and melting ice at the North and South Poles.</p><p>But guess what? Kids like you can help stop it!</p><h2>💡 Easy Ways Kids Can Help:</h2><ol><li><strong>Turn off the lights</strong> when you leave a room to save energy.</li><li><strong>Walk, bike, or scooter</strong> to school instead of riding in a car (if it’s safe!).</li><li><strong>Recycle</strong> paper, plastic, and cans so they can be used again.</li><li><strong>Plant a tree</strong> or help take care of a garden. Plants clean the air!</li><li><strong>Use less water</strong> by turning off the faucet while brushing your teeth.</li><li><strong>Tell others!</strong> Share what you know about helping the Earth with friends and family.</li></ol><h2>🌎 Your Voice Matters</h2><p>Some kids write letters to leaders or start school projects to spread awareness. You don’t have to be a grown-up to make a big impact!</p><p>Remember: <strong>You’re never too small to help make a big change.</strong> Every action counts when it comes to protecting our home—Earth!</p>', 'Featured Article: Title Goes Here (Sample Item)', '98d4b2c9-37f6-46e4-8508-12e7cf99ff10', 'a8a85575-eae0-44f2-8c5a-00405a3134f5', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1649972904349-6e44c42644a7', 'published', NULL, '2025-06-01 15:37:21.145223+00', '2025-06-01 15:37:21.145223+00', 'standard', false, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('40fb25e8-b4e8-4337-b693-be7f611f9a1d', 'Test Debate ', 'test-debate-93353396-h5pe9', '<p>Test Debate&nbsp;</p>', '', '98d4b2c9-37f6-46e4-8508-12e7cf99ff10', '43ad315b-008f-43b2-9de0-f44d84bf8ff9', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6', 'published', NULL, '2025-06-01 15:55:53.443914+00', '2025-06-01 15:55:53.443914+00', 'debate', false, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('fb7eb67b-4ca8-456a-a3c2-97a86705f905', 'Featured Article Test #2', 'featured-article-test-2-93244346-dxrjh', '<p>Featured Article Test #2</p>', 'Featured Article Test #2', '98d4b2c9-37f6-46e4-8508-12e7cf99ff10', 'a8a85575-eae0-44f2-8c5a-00405a3134f5', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6', 'published', NULL, '2025-06-01 15:54:04.451002+00', '2025-06-01 15:54:04.451002+00', 'standard', false, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('4cd1fa23-c901-4bbf-8158-65f659af86be', 'How E-Bikes Affect Our Community', 'how-ebikes-affect-our-community-69175549-1foqf', '<p class="ql-align-center">E- Bikes Affecting Kids Today&nbsp;</p><p>E-bikes can affect us kids and people in general both positively and negatively. While they offer lots of amazing things, they are also becoming known as a potential worldwide health hazard. E-bikes are causing many injuries to kids, both physically and mentally. In some places, e-bikes are banned, while in others, their use is highly regulated and watched carefully. Stricter rules are in place but it is still very unsafe. Doctors have treated children who have been seriously injured because of these electric bikes. Despite all this, the use of e-bikes continues to rise, and they are particularly popular among kids.</p><p>E-bikes also have a very positive and encouraging effect. They allow riders to travel longer distances with much less effort, which is especially helpful when climbing hills. Additionally, e-bikes contribute to reducing pollution in the air, as they provide an eco-friendly alternative to cars. E-bikes were originally designed to make travel easier and have a positive environmental impact, and they have achieved that goal. However, they also bring about challenges.</p><p>E-bikes can be difficult to control, and accidents can happen at any time. Two kids could collide with each other, and even with a helmet, the consequences can be fatal or deadly. As a kid myself, I understand the desire or want for freedom and independence, but e-bikes may not always be the safest or best option. Another issue is that some kids do not follow traffic rules. Lots of them are unsafe and do not even know what happens on the road. I myself have seen kids on the road just doing whatever they like, not paying attention to what''s around them. Lots of kids lack spacial awareness.&nbsp;They may be influenced by their peers to perform stunts on e-bikes, which they are not experienced enough to handle.</p><p>Additionally, the safety regulations for e-bikes are not always safe. In classes one and two for e-bikes, helmets are not required. This means a bike traveling over 26 miles per hour can be ridden without proper head protection.&nbsp;In the Hermosa Beach law district it states that any juvenile rider under 18 would have to pay a fine for not properly using a helmet. They also may only carry enough riders per seat. The word they specifically use is “unsafe.” I personally think it is a broad term. Unsafe could mean one thing to me but something completely different.&nbsp;On the other hand, e-bikes do encourage kids to get outside and get some exercise, as they allow them to enjoy fresh air while traveling.</p><p>However, because e-bikes are powered by electricity, there is a risk that kids may become overly dependent on technology for transportation. Traditional biking or walking encourages physical activity, while the motor assistance of an e-bike makes it easier to avoid using effort. As a result, kids may engage in less physical exercise than they would with a regular bike or by walking, which can contribute to a less engaged lifestyle. It''s important for kids to find a balance and not rely solely on e-bikes for all their transportation needs. We should play sports and find more active ways to have fun. As kids we have freedom and the chance to do what we want. We should embarace it and take advantage of it before it is gone.&nbsp;</p><p>Despite the advantages, e-bikes can present significant safety risks, especially for younger riders. Since e-bikes can reach higher speeds than traditional bicycles, there is an increased risk of accidents and collisions. Children may not have the experience or reflexes to safely navigate busy streets, sharp turns, or sudden obstacles. Without proper safety gear, such as helmets and knee pads, the risk of injury can be high. The majority&nbsp;of parents do not understand the hazards of an E-bike or what their child does with it. But still parents and guardians must ensure that children use proper safety equipment and ride responsibly to minimize these risks. From the police’s point of view, here are some opinions. The first officer I spoke to said there are lots of e-bikes, and the majority of kids who ride them are in junior high or high school. She said that some of her biggest concerns are kids not following road rules. She also said kids do not always respect the people around them, and that e-bikes should only be ridden by kids if they are used properly. The other officer I spoke to said he had many concerns about e-bikes. He thinks they are not safe at all because when kids don’t follow the rules, there is only one winner—it’s the car. He mentioned that he had been at an e-bike crash scene, and it was not fun. He wants kids to be safe and thinks it has become one of the biggest problems in the area. The police are now waiting for better rules to be put in place.</p><p>From the kids’ point of view, I spoke with a middle school boy who said he loves e-bikes and thinks they are very beneficial. He mentioned that e-bikes are helpful for getting to school when a parent is at work, getting to sports practice, or just hanging out with friends. However, he did say that most of his friends are unsafe—they don’t wear helmets, ride up hills on one wheel, and do other stunts. Another kid I spoke with was a high school girl who also loves e-bikes. She said she feels extra safe because she took a class for it at MiraCosta High School. The police also referred to this class. She mentioned that most of her friends are safe on e-bikes, but other kids are not. Overall, she believes e-bikes are safe as long as you follow the rules.</p><p>Now that you’ve heard the pros and cons of e-bikes, why don’t you share some of your opinions about these electric bikes?</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>', '', '98d4b2c9-37f6-46e4-8508-12e7cf99ff10', 'a8a85575-eae0-44f2-8c5a-00405a3134f5', '', 'published', NULL, '2025-07-21 03:39:35.989718+00', '2025-07-21 03:39:35.989718+00', 'standard', false, NULL, NULL, NULL),
