	('799a5856-ba06-46be-b50a-cbd66b4e8742', 'Pokemon is Still Going Strong ', 'pokemon-is-still-going-strong-69423472-r2h38', '<p>Pokemon is a superb fan game designed for people of all ages. First, we''re going to dive into the history, and then we''ll get to some never-released details. The founder of Pokemon is Satoshi Tajiri (referred to as Satosi Tajni in the notes). Tajiri was born on August 28, 1965, and grew up in Tokyo. He loved catching bugs and insects. When Tajiri was in high school, he was introduced to video games by an arcade hall. This inspired him to create a video game shop called Game Freaks, which was a big accomplishment because, at that time, video games were not common. Okay, that''s enough about the old style.</p><p>Now, let''s talk about the new releases. The newest set of Pokemon cards is "Stellar Chow," which has 175 cards. The most expensive card in this set is "Terepages ex Special Tristrashon repre." Additionally, there''s the newest Chinese set, "Thismatic Eye Lousons," which has 180 cards. The most expensive card in this set is "Sunbreon," also known as "Concx." In my opinion, Pokemon is the most fun game I have ever played. I like it because of the joy it brings. If you pull a really good card, you''re just so happy. It''s all about the experience, even if you don''t pull a rare card. It makes me want to open more and more packs. And if you open a super rare card, you''re just so happy and grateful.</p><p>I''ve already said this once, but I''ll say it again: Pokemon is the most fun fan game ever. Thank you for reading this. I''ll see you next time.</p><p><br></p><p class="ql-align-center"><br></p>', '', '98d4b2c9-37f6-46e4-8508-12e7cf99ff10', '79a11fa0-8250-492a-8d75-64e2682bb16d', 'https://wxmtfsexxhkjwgrejmji.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/media/images/98d4b2c9-37f6-46e4-8508-12e7cf99ff10/1753830810354_Pokemon_Wallpaper.jpg', 'published', NULL, '2025-07-21 03:43:43.702434+00', '2025-07-29 23:13:34.878984+00', 'standard', true, NULL, NULL, NULL);
